<BaseLayout locale="en" pageKey="privacy" title="Privacy Policy" description="Technical requests, embedded maps and optional analytics on the independent Supadio guide."><main id="konten" class="container-site max-w-4xl py-16"><a href="/en/" class="font-bold underline">Back to guide</a><h1 class="mt-8 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1><p class="mt-4 text-ink/65">19 October 2026</p><article class="prose-legal mt-8"><h2>Actual site interfaces</h2><p>This site has no account, booking, ticket sales, contact form or email address for sending data. Operator and airline links lead to third-party services.</p><h2>Technical data</h2><p>The hosting provider may process IP addresses, browsers and page requests to deliver and protect the service. Analytics choices are stored in the browser, not a customer profile on this site.</p><h2>Google Maps</h2><p>Embedded maps on both homepages load when the map section is approached and make requests to Google. Technical data may reach the provider separately from this site’s analytics choice. Read Google’s privacy policy.</p><h2>Analytics choices</h2><p>Google Analytics loads only after an explicit analytics choice. It may use cookies and usage data and is not described as anonymous. A tab-session refusal overrides old permission if a permanent write fails. If session storage cannot be read, analytics stays off. Settings messages explain storage limitations.</p><h2>Browser controls</h2><p>Reject or withdraw analytics in Cookie Settings, or clear site data and cookies in your browser. Language links do not store language preferences. The site code does not enable marketing tracking.</p><p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy</a> · <a href="/en/cookie-settings/">Cookie Settings</a></p></article></main></BaseLayout>